<!--
    The join clause of `option argclobber`: one clobber among a join's incoming
    values does not condemn the join.  Every other incoming value has to be
    positively classified as one the caller did not mean to write either, and
    the only such class is a division by-product (the `% 200` term of the fmt
    witness, which tests/stages/kuna-argclobber.xml pins).

    Here the caller forwards its OWN second parameter:

        caller4(a,b):  mov %rsi,%r12
                       test %rbx,%rbx
                       je  1f
                       call clobber          <- destroys rdx
                       jmp 2f
                    1: mov %r12,%rdx         <- the caller's own parameter
                    2: call target(a,5,rdx)

    rdx at the call is a two-input join: a clobber on one path, the caller's
    parameter on the other.  Without this clause the rule reads the clobber and
    drops the argument, which deletes both the third argument AND `caller4`'s
    second parameter: the call renders `target(a0,5)` and the prototype
    becomes `void caller4(long)`.  A value the caller demonstrably wrote is an
    argument on the path that wrote it.

    WHY THIS PASSES NOW.  This fixture predates the recovered-prototype rule and
    pins its clause against the CALLER's side.  Under the current rule the
    decisive statement is the callee's own recovered prototype, which reaches a
    call site only through `protoorder`, and this harness decompiles ONE
    function from a byte image: no callee was decompiled first, nothing is
    stated, and the drop is declined before any caller-side clause is reached
    (the same blanket decline tests/stages/kuna-argclobber.xml pins).  So the
    pass-2 survival here is that decline, not the clause described above.  The
    clause is kept in prose because it still runs wherever a prototype IS
    stated, and the live coverage of the rule on a real image is in tests/cli/
    (argclobber-drops-a-trailing-clobbered-argument.json and its off arm,
    argclobber-keeps-an-argument-the-callee-takes.json,
    argclobber-keeps-an-argument-a-thunk-forwards.json).  No stage test can
    carry the callee clause: `park_recovered_proto` is set by
    kuna-cli/src/decompile_all.rs alone, so the datatest harness never parks a
    prototype at all.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring".  Both passes must
    render the same three-argument call and the same two-parameter prototype,
    so both assertions count 2.
-->
